            "text": "Here's the information about Alberto Carbonell from his profile:\n\n**Profile**\n- **Name:** Alberto Carbonell\n- **Title:** Senior Software Engineer — AI Agents & Full-Stack TypeScript\n- **Location:** Spain · Remote\n- **Tagline:** Senior engineer, 10+ years with TypeScript, Node.js and PostgreSQL. I build AI agents that do real work end to end.\n\n**Work Experience**\n1. **CoverWallet** (2019 — now) – Senior Software Engineer, Madrid/Remote\n   - Insurtech platform integrating external insurance carriers\n   - Led cross-team projects in React, Node.js/TypeScript and Ruby on Rails\n   - Introduced AI agents into engineering workflow\n\n2. **M&GT Consulting** (2016 — 2019) – Software Developer, Madrid\n   - Built REST APIs and web/mobile apps for international clients\n   - Delivered blockchain solutions on Hyperledger Fabric and Ethereum\n\n3. **Indra** (2015 — 2016) – Software Developer, A Coruña\n   - Java/Spring and Oracle PL/SQL for telecom clients; QA and hotfixes\n\n**AI Agent Projects**\n- **Fraud Detection Agent** (offline-evals): Reviews events on a ticketing platform. Graded autonomy with offline evals showing 86% accuracy vs 71%, reducing fraud approved without human review from 27% to 0%.\n- **Organizer Support Agent** (coming-soon): Answers event organizers' questions about sales, payouts and setup using live data from PostgreSQL and payments API.\n- **Portfolio Agent** (personal-project): Agent on the portfolio site that answers visitors' questions about experience and projects in natural language; also exposed as an MCP server.\n\n**Tech Stack**\n- **AI/agents:** Claude, Grok, Open-source models (cloud and local via Ollama), Tool calling, MCP, Agent evals and monitoring\n- **Languages:** TypeScript, JavaScript, Ruby\n- **Backend & data:** Node.js, NestJS, Express, Next.js, REST, GraphQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB\n- **Infra:** Docker, Kubernetes, CircleCI, Vercel, Railway, Neon, GCP\n- **Frontend:** React, React Native, Angular\n\n**Education**\n- Higher Technical Diplomas (CFGS) in Web Development, Multiplatform Development and Systems Administration at CIFP Rodolfo Ucha Piñeiro (2010 — 2015), A Coruña\n\n**Languages**\n- Spanish (Native), English (C1)",
